<title>ITALY: Italy's Perugia sees Jan CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Perugia sees Jan CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PERUGIA, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Perugia said its January consumer price index was 0.0 percent month-on-month and 2.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In December, Perugia's inflation rate was flat and 2.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Perugia is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 1.26 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.0)    2.5 (2.8)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1    (0.0)    1.9 (2.7)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0    (0.0)    4.3 (4.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2    (0.1)    3.5 (6.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (-0.3)    0.9 (1.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		   2.1    (0.5)    3.6 (2.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.7    (0.0)    2.9 (2.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.7    (0.6)    3.4 (4.7)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    6.5 (5.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.3    (0.0)    1.2 (0.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	-0.3   (-0.3)    0.6 (0.6)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
